No, this function, as it currently exists, will not create a new document automatically if one does not yet exist. To handle the case where the document does not exist, you can use `set()` method, which creates the document if it doesn't exist, or update it if it does, instead of the `update()` method.

Here's how you can modify the function to handle cases when the document does not exist:

```kotlin
